# Class: obo:FOODON_03400643 (Codex Alimentarius classification of food and feed commodities)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400643 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400643 "Codex Alimentarius, Volume 2 - 1993, Section 2:  Pesticide Residues in Food.

The Codex Classification of food and animal feed commodities moving in trade and the description of the various items and groups of food and animal feedstuffs included in the present document have been developed by the Codex Committee on Pesticide Residues. It was first adopted by the 18th Session of the Codex Alimentarius Commission, (1989).

The Codex Classification includes food commodities and animal feedstuffs for which Codex maximum residue limits will not necessarily be established. The Classification is intended to be as complete a listing of food commodities in trade as possible, classified into groups on the basis of the commodity's similar potential for pesticide residues.

The Classification may also be appropriate for other purposes such as setting maximum levels for other types of residues or for other contaminants in food. The Codex Classification should be consulted in order to obtain a precise description of the food or animal feed commodities and, especially, in cases where Codex maximum residue limits have been set for groups of food and groups of animal feedstuffs. The Codex Classification is intended to promote harmonization of the terms used to describe commodities which are subject to maximum residue limits and of the approach to grouping commodities with similar potential for residue for which a common group maximum residue limit can be set."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400643 langual:A0643)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400643 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400643 "Codex Alimentarius classification of food and feed commodities"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400643 obo:FOODON_03400352)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400644 (a.  primary food commodities of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400644 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400644 langual:A0644)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400644 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400644 "a.  primary food commodities of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400644 obo:FOODON_03400643)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400645 (b.  primary food commodities of animal origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400645 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400645 langual:A0645)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400645 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400645 "b.  primary food commodities of animal origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400645 obo:FOODON_03400643)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400646 (c.  primary feed commodities (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400646 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400646 "Four the purpose of the Codex Alimentarius the term \"primary feed commodity\" means the product in or nearly in its natura1 state intended for sale to:

1.  the stock farmer as feed which is used without further processing for livestock animals or after silaging or similar farm processes;

2.  the animal feed industry as a raw material for preparing compounded feeds;"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400646 langual:A0646)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400646 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400646 "c.  primary feed commodities (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400646 obo:FOODON_03400643)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400647 (d.  processed food of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400647 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400647 langual:A0647)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400647 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400647 "d.  processed food of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400647 obo:FOODON_03400643)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400648 (e.  processed food of animal origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400648 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400648 langual:A0648)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400648 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400648 "e.  processed food of animal origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400648 obo:FOODON_03400643)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400649 (01  fruits (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400649 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400649 "Fruits are derived from many different kinds of perennial plants, trees and shrubs, usually cultivated. They consist mostly of the ripe, often sweet, succulent or pulpy developed plant ovary and its accessory parts, commonly and traditionally known as fruit.
Exposure to pesticides is dependent on the particular part of the fruit used for food. Fruits may be consumed whole, after the removal of the peel, or in part, and in the form of fresh, dried or processed products."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400649 langual:A0649)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400649 "01  fruits (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400649 obo:FOODON_03400644)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400650 (02  vegetables (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400650 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400650 "Vegetables are foods derived from many different kinds of plants mostly annual and usually cultivated, commonly known by custom and tradition as \"vegetables\".
In several countries, some of these commodities grown on large areas are distinguished as \"field crops\" or arable crops e.g. sugar beet. For the sake of convenience in this guide such crops are classified under Type 2 Vegetables.
Exposure to pesticides is dependent on the particular part of the plant used for food and the growing practices.
Vegetables may be consumed in whole or in part and in the form of fresh, dried or processed foods."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400650 langual:A0650)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400650 "02  vegetables (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400650 obo:FOODON_03400644)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400651 (03  grasses (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400651 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400651 "TYPE 03 - GRASSES

Grasses are herbaceous annual and perennial monocotyledonous plants of different kinds, cultivated extensively for their ears (heads) of starchy seeds used directly for the production of food. Grasses used for animal feed are classified under Class C; Primary Animal feed commodities, Group 051.

The plants are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400651 langual:A0651)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400651 "03  grasses (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400651 obo:FOODON_03400644)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400652 (04  nuts and seeds (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400652 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400652 "TYPE 04  -  NUTS AND SEEDS

Nuts and seeds are derived from a large variety of trees, shrubs and herbaceous plants, mostly cultivated.

The mature seeds or nuts are used as human food, for the production of beverages or edible vegetable oils and for the production of seed meals and cakes for animal feed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400652 langual:A0652)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400652 "04  nuts and seeds (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400652 obo:FOODON_03400644)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400653 (05  herbs and spices (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400653 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400653 "TYPE 05  -  HERBS AND SPICES

Herbs and spices are the flavoursome or aromatic leaves, stems, roots, flowers or fruits of a variety of plants used to impart special flavours to food and beverages."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400653 langual:A0653)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400653 "05  herbs and spices (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400653 obo:FOODON_03400644)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400654 (06  mammalian products (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400654 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400654 "TYPE 06  -  MAMMALIAN PRODUCTS

Mammalian products are derived from the edible parts of various mammals, primarily herbivorous, slaughtered for food. These mammals are usually domesticated, or to a lesser extent obtained as game animals.

This type does not include edible products from marine mammals, for which see Group 044."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400654 langual:A0654)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400654 "06  mammalian products (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400654 obo:FOODON_03400645)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400655 (07  poultry products (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400655 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400655 langual:A0655)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400655 "07  poultry products (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400655 obo:FOODON_03400645)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400656 (08  aquatic animal products (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400656 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400656 "Type 08  -  Aquatic animal products

Aquatic animal products are derived from the edible parts of various aquatic animals, usually wild, harvested for food."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400656 langual:A0656)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400656 "08  aquatic animal products (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400656 obo:FOODON_03400645)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400657 (09  amphibians and reptiles (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400657 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400657 langual:A0657)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400657 "09  amphibians and reptiles (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400657 obo:FOODON_03400645)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400658 (10  invertebrate animals (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400658 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400658 langual:A0658)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400658 "10  invertebrate animals (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400658 obo:FOODON_03400645)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400659 (11  primary food commodities of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400659 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400659 "Type 11  -  Primary feed commodities of plant origin

The primary feed commodities of plant origin include products after removal of certain parts of the plants.

Some types of the primary feed commodities are grown and used exclusively for animal feeding purposes, e.g. alfalfa vetch and maize forage. Other types are derived from crops of which the edible parts are used directly or after processing as food, whereas the \"waste\" parts of these crops are generally used for feeding purposes, e.g. cereal straws, pea vines (fresh = green), pea hay, maize fodder, sugar beet tops or -leaves."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400659 langual:A0659)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400659 "11  primary food commodities of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400659 obo:FOODON_03400646)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400660 (12  secondary food commodities of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400660 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400660 "The term \"secondary food commodity\" means a \"primary food commodity\" which has undergone simple processing, such as removal of certain portions, drying (except natural drying), husking, and comminution, which do not basically alter the composition or identity of the product. Natural field dried mature crops or parts of crops such as pulses, bulb onions or cereal grains are not considered as secondary food commodities.

Secondary food commodities may be processed further or used as ingredients in the manufacture of food or sold directly to the consumer."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400660 langual:A0660)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400660 "12  secondary food commodities of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400660 obo:FOODON_03400647)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400661 (13  derived products of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400661 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400661 "Type 13  -  Derived edible products of plant origin

\"Derived edible products\" are foods or edible substances isolated from primary food commodities or raw agricultural commodities, not intended for human consumption as such, using physical, biological or chemical processing.

This type of processed food includes groups such as vegetable oils (crude and refined), by-products of the fractionation of cereals fruit juices, teas (fermented and dried), cocoa powder and by-products of cocoa manufacturing, and extracts of various plants."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400661 langual:A0661)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400661 "13  derived products of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400661 obo:FOODON_03400647)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400662 (14  manufactured foods (single ingredient) of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400662 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400662 "Type 14 - Manufactured Foods (single-ingredient) of plant origin

The term \"single-ingredient manufactured food\" means a \"processed food\" which consists of one identifiable food ingredient, with or without packing medium or minor ingredients, such as flavouring agents, spices and condiments, and which is normally pre-packaged and ready for consumption with or without cooking."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400662 langual:A0662)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400662 "14  manufactured foods (single ingredient) of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400662 obo:FOODON_03400647)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400663 (15  manufactured foods (multi-ingredient) of plant origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400663 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400663 "The term \"multi-ingredient manufactured food\" means a processed food, consisting of more than one major ingredient.

A multi-ingredient food consisting of ingredients of both plant and animal origin will be included in this type if the ingredient(s) of plant origin is (are) predominant."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400663 langual:A0663)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400663 "15  manufactured foods (multi-ingredient) of plant origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400663 obo:FOODON_03400647)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400664 (16  secondary food commodities of animal origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400664 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400664 "Type 16 - Secondary food commodities of animal origin

The term \"secondary food commodity\" means a \"primary food commodity\" which has undergone simple processing, such as removal of certain portions, drying, and comminution, which do not basically alter the composition or identity of the commodity.

Secondary food commodities may be processed further, or used as ingredients in the manufacture of food, or sold directly to the consumer.

This type of processed food includes groups of processed primary food commodities of animal origin which have undergone simple processing, such as processed mammalian meat and poultry meat, fishes and other aquatic animals, e.g. dried meat, dried fish."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400664 langual:A0664)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400664 "16  secondary food commodities of animal origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400664 obo:FOODON_03400648)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400665 (17  derived edible products of animal origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400665 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400665 "Type 17 - Derived edible products of animal origin

The term \"Derived edible products\" means foods or edible substances isolated from primary food commodities or raw agricultural commodities not intended for human consumption as such, using physical, biological and chemical processes.

This type includes processed (rendered or extracted, possibly refined and/or clarified) fats from mammals, including aquatic mammals, poultry and aquatic organisms such as fishes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400665 langual:A0665)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400665 "17  derived edible products of animal origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400665 obo:FOODON_03400648)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400666 (18  manufactured food (single-ingredient) of animal origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400666 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400666 "The term \"single ingredient manufactured food\" means a processed food which consists of one identifiable food ingredient, with or without packing medium or minor ingredients such as flavouring agents, spices and condiments, and which is normally pre-packaged and ready for consumption, with or without cooking."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400666 langual:A0666)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400666 "18  manufactured food (single-ingredient) of animal origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400666 obo:FOODON_03400648)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400667 (19  manufactured food (multi-ingredient) of animal origin (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400667 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400667 "19  Manufactured food (multi-ingredient) of animal origin

The term \"multi-ingredient manufactured food\" means a processed food consisting of more than one major ingredient.
A multi-ingredient food consisting of ingredients of both animal and plant origin will be included in this type if the ingredient(s) of animal origin is (are) predominant"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400667 langual:A0667)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400667 "19  manufactured food (multi-ingredient) of animal origin (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400667 obo:FOODON_03400648)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400668 (001  citrus fruits (fc) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400668 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400668 "Citrus fruits are produced on trees or shrubs of the family Rutaceae. These fruits are characterized by aromatic oily peel, globular form and interior segments of juice-filled vesicles. The fruit is fully exposed to pesticides during the growing season. Post-harvest treatments with pesticides and liquid waxes are often carried out to avoid deterioration during transport and distribution due to fungal diseases, insect pests or loss of moisture.
The fruit pulp may be consumed in succulent form and as a juice. The entire fruit may be used for preserves."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400668 langual:A0668)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400668 "001  citrus fruits (fc) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400668 obo:FOODON_03400649)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400669 (002  pome fruits (fp) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400669 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400669 "Pome fruits are produced on trees and shrubs belonging to certain genera of the rose family (Rosaceae), especially the genera Malus and Pyrus. They are characterized by fleshy tissue surrounding a core consisting of parchment-like carpels enclosing the seeds.
Pome fruits are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season. Post-harvest treatments directly after harvest may also occur. The entire fruit, except the core, may be consumed in the succulent form or after processing."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400669 langual:A0669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400669 "002  pome fruits (fp) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400669 obo:FOODON_03400649)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400670 (003  stone fruits (fs) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400670 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400670 "Stone fruits are produced on trees belonging to the genus Prunus of the rose family (Rosaceae). They are characterized by fleshy tissue surrounding a single hard shelled seed. The fruit is fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season (fruit setting until harvest). Dipping of fruit immediately after harvest, especially with fungicides, may also occur.
The entire fruit, except the seed, may be consumed in a succulent or processed form."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400670 langual:A0670)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400670 "003  stone fruits (fs) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400670 obo:FOODON_03400649)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400671 (004  berries and other small fruits (fb) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400671 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400671 "Berries and other small fruits are derived from a variety of perennial plants and shrubs having fruit characterized by a high surface: weight ratio. The fruits are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season (blossoming until harvest).
The entire fruit, often including seed, may be consumed in a succulent or processed form."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400671 langual:A0671)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400671 "004  berries and other small fruits (fb) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400671 obo:FOODON_03400649)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400672 (005  assorted tropical and sub-tropical fruit - edible peel (ft) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400672 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400672 "The assorted tropical and sub-tropical fruits - edible peel are derived from the immature or mature fruits of a large variety of perennial plants, usually shrubs or trees. The fruits are fully exposed to pesticides during the growing season (period of fruit development).
The whole fruit may be consumed in a succulent or processed form."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400672 langual:A0672)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400672 "005  assorted tropical and sub-tropical fruit - edible peel (ft) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400672 obo:FOODON_03400649)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400673 (006  assorted tropical and sub-tropical fruit - inedible peel (fi) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400673 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400673 "The assorted tropical and sub-tropical fruits - inedible peel are derived from the immature or mature fruits of a large variety of perennial plants, usually shrubs or trees. Fruits are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season (period of fruit development) but the edible portion is protected by skin, peel or husk. The edible part of the fruits may be consumed in a fresh or processed form."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400673 langual:A0673)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400673 "006  assorted tropical and sub-tropical fruit - inedible peel (fi) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400673 obo:FOODON_03400649)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400674 (009  bulb vegetables (va) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400674 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400674 "Bulb vegetables are pungent highly flavoured foods derived from fleshy scale bulbs in some commodities including stem and leaves, of the genus Allium of the lily family (Lilaceae). Bulb fennel is included in this group; the bulb-like growth of this commodity gives rise to similar residues.
The subterranean parts of the bulbs and shoots are protected from direct exposure to pesticides during the growing season.
The entire bulb may be consumed after removal of the parchment-like skin. The leaves and stems of some species or cultivars may also be consumed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400674 langual:A0674)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400674 "009  bulb vegetables (va) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400674 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400675 (010  brassica (cole or cabbage) vegetables, head cabbage, flowerhead brassicas (vb) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400675 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400675 "Brassica (cole or cabbage) vegetables and flowerhead brassicas are foods derived from the leafy heads, stems and immature inflorescences of plants belonging to the genus Brassica or the family Cruciferae. Although Kohlrabi does not comply fully with the description above, for convenience and because of the similarity in residue behaviour the commodity is classified in this group. Koblrabi is a tuber-like enlargement of the stem.
The edible part of the crop is partly protected from pesticides applied during the growing season by outer leaves, or skin (Kohlrabi).
The entire vegetable after discarding obviously decomposed or withered leaves may be consumed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400675 langual:A0675)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400675 "010  brassica (cole or cabbage) vegetables, head cabbage, flowerhead brassicas (vb) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400675 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400676 (011  fruiting vegetables, cucurbits (vc) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400676 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400676 "Fruiting vegetables, Cucurbits are derived from the immature or mature fruits of various plants, belonging to the botanical family Cucurbitaceae; usually these are annual vines or bushes.
These vegetables are fully exposed to pesticides during the period of fruit development.
The edible portion of those fruits of which the inedible peel is discarded before consumption is protected from most pesticides, by the skin or peel, except from pesticides with a systemic action.
The entire fruiting vegetables or the edible portion after discarding the inedible peel may be consumed in the fresh form or after processing.The entire immature fruit of some of the fruiting vegetables species may be consumed, whereas only the edible portion of the mature fruit of the same species, after discarding the then inedible peel, is consumed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400676 langual:A0676)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400676 "011  fruiting vegetables, cucurbits (vc) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400676 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400677 (012  fruiting vegetables, other than cucurbits (vo) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400677 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400677 "Fruiting vegetables, other than Cucurbits are derived from the immature and mature fruits of various plants, usually annual vines or bushes. The group includes edible fungi and mushrooms, being comparable organs of lower plants. Many plants of this group belong to the botanical family Solanaceae.
This group does not include fruits of vegetables of the botanical family Cucurbitaceae or the pods of vegetables of the Leguminosae-family.
The vegetables of this group are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the period of fruit development, except those of which the edible portion is covered by husks, such as sweet corn, ground cherries (Physalis spp.). The latter fruiting vegetables are protected from most pesticides by the husk except from pesticides with a systemic action.
The entire fruiting vegetable or the edible portion after discarding husks or peels may be consumed in a fresh form or after processing."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400677 langual:A0677)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400677 "012  fruiting vegetables, other than cucurbits (vo) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400677 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400678 (013  leafy vegetables (including brassica leafy vegetables) (vl) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400678 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400678 "Leafy vegetables are foods derived from the leaves of a wide variety of edible plants, usually annuals or biennials. They are characterized by a high surface:weight ratio. The leaves are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season.
The entire leaf may be consumed, either fresh or after processing or household cooking."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400678 langual:A0678)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400678 "013  leafy vegetables (including brassica leafy vegetables) (vl) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400678 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400679 (014  legume vegetables (vp) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400679 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400679 "Legume vegetables are derived from the succulent seed and immature pods of leguminous plants commonly known as beans and peas.
Pods are fully exposed to pesticides during the growing season, whereas the succulent seed is protected within the pod from most pesticides, except pesticides with systemic action.
The succulent forms may be consumed as whole pods or as the shelled product."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400679 langual:A0679)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400679 "014  legume vegetables (vp) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400679 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400680 (015  pulses (vd) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400680 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400680 "Pulses are derived from the mature seeds naturally or artificially dried, of leguminous plants known as beans (dry) and peas (dry).
The seeds in the pods are protected from most pesticides applied during the growing season except pesticides which show a systemic action. The dried beans and peas however are often exposed to post-harvest treatments.
The dry pulses are consumed after processing or household cooking."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400680 langual:A0680)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400680 "015  pulses (vd) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400680 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400681 (016  root and tuber vegetables (vr) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400681 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400681 "Root and tuber vegetables are the starchy enlarged solid roots, tubers, corms or rhizomes, mostly subterranean, of various species of plants, mostly annuals.
The underground location protects the edible portion from pesticides applied to the aerial parts of the crop during the growing season; however the commodities in this group are exposed to pesticide residues from soil treatments.
The entire vegetable may be consumed in the form of fresh or processed foods."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400681 langual:A0681)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400681 "016  root and tuber vegetables (vr) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400681 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400682 (017  stalk and stem vegetables (vs) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400682 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400682 "Stalk and stem vegetables are the edible stalks, leaf stems or immature shoots, from a variety of annual or perennial plants. Although not actually belonging to this group, globe artichoke (the immature flowerhead) of the family Compositae is included in this group.
Depending upon the part of the crop used for consumption and the growing practices, stalk and stem vegetables are exposed, in varying degrees, to pesticides applied during the growing season.
Stalk and stem vegetables may be consumed in whole or in part and in the form of fresh, dried or processed foods."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400682 langual:A0682)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400682 "017  stalk and stem vegetables (vs) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400682 obo:FOODON_03400650)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400683 (020  cereal grains (gc) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400683 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400683 "Cereal grains are derived from the ears (heads) of starchy seeds produced by a variety of plants, primarily of the grass family (Grainineae)
Buckwheat, a dicotyledonous crop belonging to the botanical family Polygonaceae and two Chenopodium species, belonging to the botanical family Chenopodiaceae are included in this group, because of similarities in size and type of the seed, residue pattern and the use of the commodity.
The edible seeds are protected to varying degrees from pesticides applied during flee growing season by husks. Husks are removed before processing and/or consumption.
Cereal grains are often exposed to post-harvest treatments with pesticides."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400683 langual:A0683)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400683 "020  cereal grains (gc) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400683 obo:FOODON_03400651)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400684 (021  grasses for sugar and syrup production (gs) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400684 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400684 "Grasses For sugar or syrup production, includes species of grasses with a high sugar content especially in the stem. The stems are mainly used for sugar or syrup production, and to a small extent as vegetables or sweets. The leaves, ears and several wastes of the sugar or syrup manufacturing process are used, among others, as animal feed see Group 052: Miscellaneous fodder and forage crops)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400684 langual:A0684)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400684 "021  grasses for sugar and syrup production (gs) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400684 obo:FOODON_03400651)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400685 (022  tree nuts (tn) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400685 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400685 "Tree nuts are the seeds of a variety of trees and shrubs which are characterized by a hard inedible shell enclosing an oily seed.
The seed is protected from pesticides applied during the growing season by the shell and other parts of the fruit.
The edible portion of the nut is consumed in succulent, dried or processed forms."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400685 langual:A0685)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400685 "022  tree nuts (tn) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400685 obo:FOODON_03400652)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400686 (023  oilseed (so) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400686 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400686 "Oilseed consists of seeds from a variety of plants used in the production of edible vegetable oils, seed meals and cakes for animal feed. Some important vegetable oil seeds are by-products of fibre or fruit crops (e.g. cotton seed, olives).
Some of the oilseeds are, directly or after slight processing (e.g. roasting), used as food (e.g. peanuts) or for food flavouring (e.g. poppy seed, sesame seed).
Oilseeds are protected from pesticides applied during the growing season by the shell or husk."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400686 langual:A0686)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400686 "023  oilseed (so) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400686 obo:FOODON_03400652)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400687 (024  seed for beverages and sweets (sb) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400687 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400687 "The seeds for beverages and sweets are derived from tropical and sub-tropical trees and shrubs. After processing the seeds are used in the production of beverages and sweets.
These seeds are protected from pesticides applied during the growing season by the shell or other parts of the fruit."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400687 langual:A0687)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400687 "024  seed for beverages and sweets (sb) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400687 obo:FOODON_03400652)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400688 (027  herbs (hh) (ccpr))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400688 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400688 "Herbs consist of leaves, flowers, stems and roots from a variety of herbaceous plants, used in relatively small amounts as condiments to flavour foods or beverages. They are used either in fresh or naturally dried form.
Herbs are fully exposed to pesticides applied during the growing season. Post-harvest treatments are often carried out on dried herbs.
Herbs are consumed as components of other foods in succulent and dried forms or as extracts of the succulent products."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400688 langual:A0688)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400688 "027  herbs (hh) (ccpr)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400688 obo:FOODON_03400653)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400689 (028  spices (hs) (codex))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400689 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400689 "Spices consist of the aromatic seeds roots, berries or other fruits from a variety of plants, which are used in relatively small quantities to flavour foods.
Spices are exposed in varying degrees to pesticides applied during the growing season. Also post-harvest treatments may be applied to spices in the dried form.
They are consumed primarily in the dried form as condiment."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400689 langual:A0689)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400689 "028  spices (hs) (codex)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400689 obo:FOODON_03400653)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03400690 (european food groups (efg))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03400690 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03400690 "The European Food Groups (EFG) classification system was developed, as a project of COST Action 99/Eurofoods, in an attempt to evaluate the level of food description and classification that would permit international comparisons of the results of available food consumption and food availability surveys. In order to formulate the EFG system, several classification schemes used for recording food intake at the international and national classification schemes were compared:  International - FAO Food Balance Sheet, WHO GEMS/FOODS regional diets, DAFNE classification system for Household Budget Survey (HBS) data, and Eurocode 2 core classification (levels 1 and 2); National  -   French National Food Consumption Survey (1999), Dutch National Food Consumption Survey (1998), and British National Food Survey.
In the process of comparing food intake data from various European countries, it became evident that such comparisons are feasible only when results are expressed at the raw ingredient level. Since the DAFNE classification system groups food items at the raw level, it was one of the international classification schemes used to create the EFG food grouping system.
Ref.:  Ireland, J., Van Erp-Baart, A.M.J., Charrondière, U.R., Møller, A., Smithers, G., and Trichopoulou, A.: Selection of food classification system and food composition database for future food consumption surveys. European Journal of Clinical Nutrition, 56, Suppl. 2, S33 - S45, 2002."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03400690 langual:A0690)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03400690 "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03400690 "european food groups (efg)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03400690 obo:FOODON_03400356)

