# Class: obo:FOODON_03401311 (enzyme supplement)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03401311 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03401311 "Plant and animal enzymes are used to facilitate the digestive process and improve the body's ability to maintain balanced metabolism. Enzyme supplements are extracted from plants like pineapple and papaya and from the organs of cows and pigs. The supplements are typically given in tablet or capsule form. Pancreatic enzymes may also be given by injection. The dosage varies with the condition being treated. For nondigestive ailments, the supplements are taken in the hour before meals so that they can be quickly absorbed into the blood. For digestive ailments, the supplements are taken immediately before meals accompanied by a large glass of fluids. Pancreatic enzymes may be accompanied by doses of vitamin A.[http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/enzyme+therapy]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03401311 langual:A1311)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03401311 "LanguaL curation note: Currently not used in US classification of dietary supplements."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03401311 "enzyme supplement"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03401311 obo:FOODON_03401309)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03401312 (phytoestrogen supplement)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03401312 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03401312 "Phytoestrogens are weak estrogens found concentrated in soybeans. Extracted phytoestrogens are marketed in numerous forms as dietary supplements. Consumers of phytoestrogen supplements tend to be peri- and postmenopausal women looking for an alternative to hormone therapy."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03401312 langual:A1312)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03401312 "LanguaL curation note: Currently not used in US classification of dietary supplements."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03401312 "phytoestrogen supplement"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03401312 obo:FOODON_03401309)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03401313 (dietary supplement, combination)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03401313 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03401313 langual:A1313)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03401313 "LanguaL curation note: Use to index a dietary supplement that is a combination of any of the other supplement types. Whenever possible, use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03401313 "dietary supplement, combination"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03401313 obo:FOODON_03401298)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03401314 (dietary supplement, multi-vitamin/mineral)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03401314 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03401314 "A multivitamin/mineral supplement is defined in the United States as a supplement containing 3 or more vitamins and minerals but does not include herbs, hormones, or drugs, with each nutrient at a dose below the tolerable upper level determined by the Food and Drug Board and the maximum daily intake to not cause a risk for adverse health effects. (National Institutes of Health State-of-the-Science Panel. National Institutes of Health State-of-the-Science Conference Statement: multivitamin/mineral supplements and chronic disease prevention. Am J Clin Nutr 2007;85:257S-64S) [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multivitamin]

In Europe, a supplement containing 2 or more vitamins and minerals is defined as vitamin-mineral combination supplement."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03401314 "WIKIPEDIA:Multivitamin")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03401314 langual:A1314)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03401314 "dietary supplement, multi-vitamin/mineral"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03401314 obo:FOODON_03401313)

