AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542159 "The group includes any type of Hungarian-type salami, less strongly flavored -mostly with garlic and eventually paprika- and more heavily smoked than Italian salami. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_salami] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Hungarian salami]"@en)
