AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542163 "The group includes any type of Linguica sausage, also known as Longanzia, i.e. a Portuguese sausage made from coarsely ground pork butts, seasoned with paprika, garlic, cumin seeds and cinnamon, cured in vinegar pickling liquid before stuffing and smoked. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linguica_sausage] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Linguica, sausage]"@en)
