# Class: obo:FOODON_03542184 (21840 - frankfurt-type sausage (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542184 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542184 "The group includes any type of Frankfurt-type sausage. Frankfurters are traditionally made from pork and beef, but nowadays chicken and turkey are also used. The characterising ingredients should be reported with additional facet descriptors. The sizes range from big dinner frankfurters to tiny cocktail size and may be skinless or with natural casings. The terms \"frankfurter,\" \"wiener\" and \"hot dog\" are often used interchangeably. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_dog] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Frankfurt-type sausage]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542184 langual:A026B)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542184 "21840 - frankfurt-type sausage (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542184 obo:FOODON_03542180)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03542185 (21850 - frankfurter sausage (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542185 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542185 "The group includes any type of Frankfurt sausage, a product originated in Frankfurt, Germany, which consists of a combination of beef and pork or only beef. It is cured, smoked and fully cooked and usually it is served hot. Its seasonings may include coriander, garlic, ground mustard, nutmeg, salt, sugar and white pepper. The sizes range from big dinner frankfurters to tiny cocktail size and may be skinless or with natural casings. The terms \"frankfurter,\" \"wiener\" and \"hot dog\" are often used interchangeably. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_dog] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Frankfurter sausage]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542185 langual:A026C)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542185 "21850 - frankfurter sausage (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542185 obo:FOODON_03542184)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03542186 (21860 - wiener sausage (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542186 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542186 "The group includes any type of sausage marketed as Wiener or Vienna sausage, which is similar to frankfurter but usually made only from pork, smaller in diameter and softer in texture. The term 'Vienna sausage' most often applied to small, open end sausages packed in cans of water, and it may also be used interchangeably with 'wiener' or 'frankfurter'. In case of canned sausages, 'canning' should be reported with additional facet descriptors. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vienna_sausage] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Wiener sausage]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542186 langual:A026D)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03542186 "vienna sausage"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542186 "21860 - wiener sausage (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542186 obo:FOODON_03542184)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03542187 (21870 - cooked bratwurst-type sausage (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542187 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542187 "The group includes any type of Cooked bratwurst-type sausage, usually made from pork or a mixture of pork and veal/beef. For the fresh (not cooked) variants of bratwurst use the code A024N 'Fresh bratwurst'. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/bratwurst] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Cooked bratwurst sausage]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542187 langual:A026E)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542187 "21870 - cooked bratwurst-type sausage (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542187 obo:FOODON_03542180)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542187 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002351 obo:FOODON_00002993))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03542188 (21880 - beerwurst (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542188 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542188 "The group includes any type of Beerwurst, also known as Bierwurst, which is a German cooked, smoked sausage usually seasoned with mustard seeds, garlic and other spices. The meat is partially cured and then made into the sausage with the other ingredients, after which, the sausage is further cured, smoked and then blanched. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beerwurst] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Beerwurst]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542188 langual:A026F)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542188 "21880 - beerwurst (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542188 obo:FOODON_03542187)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03542189 (21890 - bockwurst (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542189 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542189 "The group includes any type of Bockwurst, i.e. a German sausage made of pork and veal usually seasoned with chives, white pepper, parsley, nutmeg (or mace) and lemon. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. The eventual removal of not edible parts is unspecified. When relevant, information on the part consumed/analysed has to be reported with additional facet descriptors.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bockwurst] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Bockwurst]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542189 langual:A026G)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542189 "21890 - bockwurst (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542189 obo:FOODON_03542187)

