# Class: obo:FOODON_03542286 (22860 - diadromous fish (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03542286 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03542286 "The group includes any type of Diadromous fish (ISSCAAP division 2), i.e. fishes that in general migrate from the sea to brackish and/or fresh water and in the opposite direction. The anadromous species spawn in fresh water (streams, small rivers and brooks) e.g. several salmon species, whereas eels spawn in the ocean. Some species, such as trout, are domesticated and do not migrate; they are bred in fish farms in ponds, mountain streams etc.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diadromous_fish] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=edible fish Diadromous fish]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03542286 langual:A028E)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03542286 "22860 - diadromous fish (efsa foodex2)"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03542286 obo:FOODON_03542212)

