# Class: obo:FOODON_03543341 (33410 - stout beer (efsa foodex2))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03543341 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03543341 "The group includes any type of stout beer. Stout is a dark beer made using roasted malt or roasted barley, hops, water and yeast. Stouts were traditionally the generic term for the strongest or stoutest porters, typically 7% or 8% produced by a brewery. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole marketed unit or a homogeneous representative portion.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stout_beer] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Stout beer]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03543341 langual:A03ML)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03543341 "33410 - stout beer (efsa foodex2)"@en)
