AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03543945 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03543945 "The group includes any type of quiche. In French cuisine, a quiche is an oven-baked dish usually made with eggs, milk or cream and other ingredients (e.g. vegetables, meat products, etc.) in a pastry crust. More detailed information on the characterising ingredients can be added with additional facet descriptors. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole marketed unit or a homogeneous representative portion.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quiche] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm=isch&q=Quiche]"@en)
